Task 5: Advanced Content View Management
Subtask 5.1: Create Content View with CLI
You can also manage content views using the command line interface:

Access Satellite CLI:

# SSH to your Satellite server
ssh root@satellite.example.com

# List existing content views
hammer content-view list --organization "Default Organization"
Create Content View via CLI:

# Create a new content view
hammer content-view create \
  --name "RHEL8-Security-CV" \
  --description "RHEL 8 Security Updates Only" \
  --organization "Default Organization"

# Add repository to content view
hammer content-view add-repository \
  --name "RHEL8-Security-CV" \
  --organization "Default Organization" \
  --repository "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8 for x86_64 - BaseOS RPMs 8"
Publish Content View:

# Publish the content view
hammer content-view publish \
  --name "RHEL8-Security-CV" \
  --organization "Default Organization" \
  --description "Initial security-focused version"
Subtask 5.2: Automate Content Promotion
Create Promotion Script:

# Create automation script
cat > /root/promote_content.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# Variables
ORG="Default Organization"
CV_NAME="RHEL8-BaseOS-CV"

# Get latest version
LATEST_VERSION=$(hammer content-view version list \
  --content-view "$CV_NAME" \
  --organization "$ORG" \
  --fields "Version" | tail -n 1 | awk '{print $1}')

# Promote through environments
for ENV in "Development" "Testing" "Production"; do
  echo "Promoting $CV_NAME version $LATEST_VERSION to $ENV"
  hammer content-view version promote \
    --content-view "$CV_NAME" \
    --organization "$ORG" \
    --to-lifecycle-environment "$ENV" \
    --version "$LATEST_VERSION"
done
EOF

# Make script executable
chmod +x /root/promote_content.sh
Test Automation Script:

# Run the promotion script
/root/promote_content.sh
